B08d genuine shared-loader closure, 2026-09-27
============================================

The five unchanged libc-test programs are the minimal original consumers:
functional/dlopen, functional/tls_align, functional/tls_align_dlopen,
functional/tls_init_dlopen, regression/tls_get_new-dtv.
The four original DSO fixture sources, test objects and libtest.a are GCC-built
reference harness code, not claimed as EvoCC target-C coverage.

Durable adapter: tools/ladder/musl_shared.py, invoked by tools/ladder/musl.py
after restoring reference objects and validating a static candidate set.
No second source clone, large disk, altered assertions, timeout increase or
installed-archive replacement. The configured upstream Makefile provides exact
shared-library recipes; only dlstart.c/dynlink.c are additional library compiles.
Original ELF link arguments are preserved for the library. Test executables use
the actual new loader as PT_INTERP, verified by readelf, and the original
reference-built five-second supervisor. These are real dlopen/TLS executions.

