7b95dfa5f5d5ca4d949221e0228ccc290bacc14e remain unchanged.

First bounded prototype: five reference and five candidate programs PASS.
The durable adapter independently repeats all ten executions: 10 PASS / 0 FAIL.
Eight fixture DSOs compile/link; both new EvoCC loader TUs emit/assemble/link.

Composition: 1351 linked library objects, independently recorded by path/hash.
  1268 previously accepted EvoCC C objects (hash-verified, no recompilation)
  + 2 newly EvoCC-compiled loader C objects
  + 68 reference C objects (floating complex still refused; L04)
  + 13 reference-assembled original AArch64 assembly sources.
The three static CRT C objects are not DSO library inputs. Thus the separate
shared target-C population is 1270 EvoCC / 1338, not a new 1339-unit static run.
Every candidate input is rehashed after linking and after execution. Missing or
extra accepted inputs, refused loader units, partial/duplicate test populations,
wrong/static loader, missing object/binary identity and process failure cannot
produce a shared PASS. The common bench also requires matching compiler,
composition and execution identities before a future full musl PASS.

